---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Visual Models" description="Mechanical visualizations mapping temporal flow, the CMB boundary, and universal evolution.">
  <article class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <h1>Visual Models</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Mechanical visualizations mapping temporal flow, the CMB boundary, and universal evolution. 
      These diagrams and interactive models illustrate the substrate mechanics of the AETT TSC Roberts Vacuum Model 
      without introducing new theoretical claims.
    </p>
    
    <!-- Models Grid -->
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem;">
      
      <!-- Model 1: CMB Boundary -->
      <a href="/visual-models/cmb-boundary/" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
        <div class="model-card">
          <div class="card-icon">🌌</div>
          <h3>CMB as Temporal Origin (T=0)</h3>
          <p>Why measurable time begins at recombination, and the nature of the pre-temporal void beyond the observable boundary.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Explore Model →</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- Model 2: Pulse Propulsion -->
      <a href="/visual-models/pulse-propulsion/" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
        <div class="model-card">
          <div class="card-icon">🚀</div>
          <h3>Temporal Pulse Propulsion</h3>
          <p>How pulsing acceleration resets temporal drag, allowing a vessel to decouple from the timeline and step past the light-speed barrier.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Explore Model →</span>
        </div>
      </a>

            <!-- Model 3: Flowline Mechanics -->
      <a href="/visual-models/flowlines/" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
        <div class="model-card">
          <div class="card-icon">🔦</div>
          <h3>Flowline Mechanics &amp; Temporal Drag</h3>
          <p>Visualizing the searchlight analogy. The beam is the temporal direction; the object is mass. The trailing shadow represents the resistance wake created as matter interacts with the substrate.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Explore Model →</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- Model 4: Temporal Bulge / Gravity -->
      <a href="/visual-models/temporal-bulge/" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
        <div class="model-card">
          <div class="card-icon">🕳️</div>
          <h3>The Temporal Bulge (Gravity)</h3>
          <p>Mass obstructing temporal flow, creating a forward-facing resistance wake. Gravity is not a well, but an outward bulge into the Timeless Sea driven by pressure differentials.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Explore Model →</span>
        </div>
      </a>

    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Card Styling (Scoped to this page) -->
  <style>
    .model-card {
      background: var(--bg-secondary);
      padding: 2rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
      height: 100%;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .model-card:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      transform: translateY(-4px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.15);
    }

    .card-icon {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .model-card h3 {
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text-primary);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .model-card p {
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      flex-grow: 1; /* Pushes the link to the bottom */
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .card-link {
      color: var(--accent);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }

    .model-card:hover .card-link {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>